+{"id":"frankensim-material-reality-ui2if.3.1.2","title":"Wire material capacity through theta heat integration and its adjoint","description":"Reuse the existing sourced density/Cp and capacity assignment in the native theta/Crank-Nicolson forward and source-scale adjoint. Correct fixed-boundary source differentiation and use admitted temperatures. This bounded continuation uses already implemented constant-capacity owners; broader nonlinear enthalpy and upstream source portfolios remain separate.","acceptance_criteria":"Material-only capacity substitutions affect forward heating/diffusion and the same discrete source gradient; focused analytical, heterogeneous and source-support regressions pass.","notes":"Implementation committed directly to main: 7fb1ca17948951e325b6a856d3f581a34f6fe02c. Shared transient::HeatCapacity now drives history, theta/Crank-Nicolson and its exact source-scale adjoint through the original lumped storage preparation. The combined material-bound forward/adjoint path validates source domains at initial, prescribed and accepted temperatures. Fixed the derivative to exclude Robin/Neumann environmental heat. Added analytical material-swap, heterogeneous-ID, boundary finite-difference and domain/cancellation regressions. Available nightly-2026-08-31 rustfmt parsing/formatting and focused git diff --check passed. Native cargo test -p fs-conduction --test material_heat_capacity --test transient --test thermal_history_capacity is pending the seven missing pinned constellation siblings and shared-disk capacity. Remains in_progress; no broad MR19 closure or native test success is claimed.","status":"in_progress","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-10-26T01:16:04.605421279Z","created_by":"frankensim-integration-agent","updated_at":"2026-10-26T01:32:24.978656312Z","source_repo":"frankensim","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["material-integration","material-reality-2026"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"frankensim-materia